 on his stock trading, including claims tied to Medicaid votes.\n\nCognetti has out-raised the incumbent and holds a cash-on-hand edge, while Bresnahan faces sustained outside opposition. Limited public polling from Democratic-sponsored pollsters shows narrow Cognetti leads. The race is rated a Democratic lean, but with wide uncertainty given the district's partisan lean and the incumbent's incumbency advantage.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5916, "margin": 1.42}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6449, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6453, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6734, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.617, "margin": 2.4}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6201, "margin": 2.5}]}